FINAL ANSWER:
Ben Ramsey wrote most of the code as it stands today: about 66% of the lines in `src/` and 53% in `tests/`. Nobody else who wrote a large share has touched the code since 2020, so if Ben left, almost all of the knowledge would leave with him.

I measured this by who last wrote each surviving line (`git blame -w -M -C`), not by commit counts. I also corrected for a few things in the history that would otherwise give credit to the wrong people.

## What I corrected for
- **Two email addresses for Ben:** the `.mailmap` file merges `<email redacted>` into `<email redacted>`. The same file merges "T. Wrona" into Tomasz Wrona.
- **A squashed pull request:** commit `96dd608` (Grouping) is under Ben's name, but its message says the original author is Katarzyna Nowak. I credited those 150 lines to her.
- **A co-authored commit:** `4a02cef` (#128) has Frank van den Brink as co-author, covering 41 lines.
- **Mechanical commits I skipped:** the php-cs-fixer bot run (`3b40daf`) and Tomasz's rename of the Tool namespace to Support (`c3611fa`). Both change many lines without adding any code.
- **A generated file I left out:** `src/Generated/TypeMap.php` (295 lines). It's marked `@generated`, so the T. Wrona commit that added it isn't real authorship.

## Who wrote the surviving code

| Author | src/ (3,175 lines) | tests/ (3,625 lines) | Last active in src/tests |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Ben Ramsey** | 2,093 (66%) | 1,907 (53%) | 2026-08 |
| Carlos C Soto | 275 (9%) | 208 (6%) | 2016 |
| zf2timo | 225 (7%) | 174 (5%) | 2016 |
| icanhazstring | 202 (6%) | 596 (16%) | 2019 |
| Kévin Gomez | 145 (5%) | 329 (9%) | 2018 |
| Katarzyna (Kasia) Nowak | 93 (3%) | 59 (2%) | 2026-05 |
| Tomasz Wrona | 51 (2%) | 53 (1%) | 2026-07 |
| Simone Todaro | 29 | 113 (3%) | 2020 |
| Others (~10 people) | <25 each | <100 each | — |

"Kasia Nowak <kasia@nowak.example>" and "Katarzyna Nowak <…noreply.github.com>" are almost certainly the same person, but the `.mailmap` doesn't link them. I counted them together; it's worth confirming and adding a line to the `.mailmap`.

## If Ben left
He is the main loss by a wide margin:
- **Core code is almost entirely his:** `AbstractCollection`, `AbstractArray`, `AbstractMap`, `CollectionInterface`, `QueueInterface`, `DoubleEndedQueueInterface`, `MapInterface`, `NamedParameterMap`, `TypeTrait`, `ValueExtractorTrait`, and all the static-analysis type tests in `tests/types/*`. In most of these he wrote 70–98% of the lines.
- **No one else covers those areas today.** The second-tier authors (Carlos C Soto, zf2timo, icanhazstring, Kévin Gomez) wrote real pieces, such as `TypedMap`, `Queue`, `DoubleEndedQueue`, `Set` and their tests, but they last worked on the code in 2016–2019.
- **The only other active contributors own narrow pieces:** Tomasz Wrona wrote `ChunkTrait` plus some mechanical renames, and Katarzyna Nowak wrote `Grouping`. Neither has worked on the core collection, map or queue code.
- **Ben's own recent work is light.** His last change to `src/` was a docblock reword in August 2026. He's the owner, but not working on it heavily right now.

For the handover, I'd plan knowledge-transfer time with Ben on the abstract base classes, the map/typed-map hierarchy, and the PHPStan/Psalm type tests. Tomasz Wrona and Katarzyna Nowak are worth keeping in touch with as secondary contacts for the newest features.

