**The raw history overstates some people:**
- Ben's commit counts include work he squashed for others. The real number is a little lower but still dominant.
- Tomasz Wrona has made most of the recent changes, but his own code is about 100 lines (`ChunkTrait` and its test). The rest is a rename and a generated file.
- The bots and dependabot wrote no code that survives today.

**If Ben left:**
- He wrote about two thirds of the library's code and over half its tests. He's the main author of about 10 of the 32 source files; I didn't remove PR #57 from that file count, so it may be 9.
- The other big contributors (Carlos C Soto, zf2timo, icanhazstring, Kévin Gomez) last touched `src/` or `tests/` between 2016 and 2019, so they're not around to ask.
- The only recent people are Tomasz Wrona (July 2026) and Kasia Nowak (May 2026). Each knows one feature, not the core classes.
- Ben's last real code fix was in March 2025. Since then he's only merged the squashed PR and reworded a docblock (August 2026), so even his memory of the details may be fading.

Before the handover, I'd spend time with Ben going through the core abstract classes (`AbstractArray`, `AbstractCollection`, `AbstractSet`, the maps and queues). I'd also add Kasia Nowak's two addresses to `.mailmap` so future counts show her as one person.

